---
// Chef Line's Journey: the short version of the old game-dev case study.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Wall from '../../layouts/Wall.astro';
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
import onion from '../../assets/chef-line-onion.png';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<Wall
  title="Chef Line’s Journey · Leandro Bonora"
  description="A food-themed action adventure made during my internship at Ember Glitch. Scrum master for a team of six, enemy AI with state machines and most of the UI."
>
  <article>
    <header class="wrap case-head">
      <p class="back"><a href={`${base}#work`}><Arrow dir="left" /> Back</a></p>
      <h1 class="case-title">Chef Line’s Journey</h1>
      <p class="case-summary">
        A chef ends up in a world made of food and has to fight or cook his way out. Made during my first
        internship, at game studio Ember Glitch.
      </p>
      <p class="case-meta">Scrum master and programmer · Feb – Jun 2024 · Team of six · Unity, C#</p>
    </header>

    <div class="wrap">
      <video class="clip" src={`${base}media/chef-line-gameplay.mp4`} controls preload="metadata" playsinline>
        <a href={`${base}media/chef-line-gameplay.mp4`}>Watch the gameplay video</a>
      </video>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap case-body">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Scrum master for two developers and four artists, with mentors from the studio.</li>
          <li>
            Wrote a big part of the 30+ page{' '}
            <a href={`${base}media/chef-line-gdd.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">game design document</a>{' '}
            before we built anything.
          </li>
          <li>Built the enemy AI: idle, roaming, chasing, attacking and fleeing, each as its own state.</li>
          <li>Did most of the UI, the health system and the interactive objects.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why state machines</h2>
        <p>
          My earlier enemies had everything in one script. Splitting each behaviour into its own state made the code
          readable for the other developer, and a new enemy became mostly a matter of reusing states. This is the base
          every enemy runs on:
        </p>
        <pre><code>{`public void GoToState(Type type)
{
    _currentState?.Deactivate();

    var next = GetComponentInChildren(type) as State
        ?? new GameObject(type.Name).AddComponent(type) as State;

    next.Machine = this;
    next.Activate();
    _currentState = next;
}`}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <figure class="shot">
        <Image src={onion} alt="The chef facing an onion enemy with a health bar in Chef Line’s Journey" widths={[480, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 380px" />
        <figcaption>An onion critter: it roams, spots you, chases and attacks.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <nav class="wrap case-next" aria-label="Next">
      <a href="mailto:bonoraleandro@gmail.com">Got a project in mind? Email me <Arrow /></a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</Wall>

<style>
  .case-head {
    padding-block: clamp(32px, 6vw, 80px) clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px);
  }

  .back {
    font-weight: 650;
    margin-bottom: clamp(24px, 4vw, 48px);
  }

  .back a,
  .case-next a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .case-title {
    font-size: var(--fs-display);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .case-summary {
    margin-top: 22px;
    max-width: 48ch;
    font-size: var(--fs-lede);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .case-meta {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .clip {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 960px;
    background: var(--ink);
    box-shadow: var(--note-shadow);
  }

  .case-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(280px, 380px);
    gap: clamp(40px, 7vw, 104px);
    align-items: start;
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 88px);
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: 64ch;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-subtitle);
    margin: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px) 0 14px;
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .prose li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 30px;
  }

  .prose li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.45em;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    background: var(--orange);
    transform: rotate(-4deg);
  }

  pre {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    background: #fff;
    box-shadow: var(--note-shadow);
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .shot {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 10px 10px 14px;
    background: #fff;
    box-shadow: var(--note-shadow);
    transform: rotate(1.5deg);
  }

  .shot figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .case-next {
    padding-bottom: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px);
    font-size: var(--fs-subtitle);
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .case-body {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
